  "summary": "Some white dwarfs with helium atmospheres show hydrogen, and its origin has been debated. A simple model with both internal and accreted sources was tested against DESI and SDSS samples of DB white dwarfs, requiring at least 22 +/- 2 percent to have accreted it from ices or hydrated minerals. The result depends on the model and applies to a limited temperature range.",
